WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.008 --> 00:00:05.032
(groovy electronica music)

00:00:05.032 --> 00:00:06.019
- Your hands are really dextrous things,

00:00:06.019 --> 00:00:09.376
we use them everyday
for all sorts of tasks.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:11.838
To make the best use
we possibly can of that

00:00:11.838 --> 00:00:14.011
is to build a puppet around the hands,

00:00:14.011 --> 00:00:17.747
so knuckles become knees, or elbows.

00:00:17.747 --> 00:00:19.599
So, by the end of the
day, it's all the illusion

00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:20.599
of movement.

00:00:21.877 --> 00:00:25.367
My name's Barnaby Dixion, I'm a puppeteer.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.450
That alright?

00:00:28.386 --> 00:00:31.745
I'm 26 years old, and I
started making puppets,

00:00:31.745 --> 00:00:32.912
two years ago.

00:00:35.069 --> 00:00:37.055
This is Dabchick.

00:00:37.055 --> 00:00:40.740
This is the first puppet I ever made.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.823
This is Manu.

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:47.341
And it takes two hands
to operate this puppet.

00:00:47.341 --> 00:00:48.363
And this is the dinosaur,

00:00:48.363 --> 00:00:50.112
I think this is the most expressive puppet

00:00:50.112 --> 00:00:51.112
that I have.

00:00:54.665 --> 00:00:56.933
I make them in my room, really.

00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:59.601
Each of these puppets represents
maybe two months work,

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:02.028
and it's a process
that's driven completely

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.288
by trial and error.

00:01:04.288 --> 00:01:05.503
The materials to make these puppets,

00:01:05.503 --> 00:01:07.232
I usually can just get them online,

00:01:07.232 --> 00:01:09.887
raw bits of metal or plumbers' apoxy,

00:01:09.887 --> 00:01:13.210
just things like that, really.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.166
Hey, Barnaby Dixon here.

00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:16.762
I made the puppets
originally with the purpose

00:01:16.762 --> 00:01:19.633
to create video content on youTube.

00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:21.167
Check this out.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.449
Most weeks I'll take
Dabchick out for an outing

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:24.617
where I'll film it.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.647
Ah, the great British seaside.

00:01:26.647 --> 00:01:29.939
Soft, wet sand, oh joy of joys!

00:01:29.939 --> 00:01:32.202
I always do try and make them funny.

00:01:32.202 --> 00:01:36.369
The proud fury of the waves,
thundering to their port.

00:01:37.459 --> 00:01:39.849
I do get self-conscious
about having the puppets

00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:41.359
out and about.

00:01:41.359 --> 00:01:44.406
Some people just think I'm
an adult playing with a toy.

00:01:44.406 --> 00:01:47.924
People kind of don't
know what to think of it.

00:01:47.924 --> 00:01:51.591
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.156
So, recently, I was on
a German talent show,

00:01:56.156 --> 00:01:57.983
that was about puppets,

00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:00.483
it was called Die Puppenstars.

00:02:01.442 --> 00:02:03.383
And I ended up winning this.

00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:04.567
It was very validating,

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:06.725
and so I think, yeah, a lot
of people would think

00:02:06.725 --> 00:02:09.289
it is quite a weird
thing for a 26-year-old

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:11.955
to be in his bedroom, making puppets,

00:02:11.955 --> 00:02:14.858
but it's working out for me, so,

00:02:14.858 --> 00:02:17.525
hah! (laughing)

00:02:21.782 --> 00:02:24.365
(ambient tone)

